# Redis ACL (security audit SEC-05). docker/gen-secrets.sh renders this file to docker/secrets/redis-users.acl,
# replacing the placeholder with the SHA-256 of REDIS_PASSWORD (Redis compares hashes; the plain password is not in
# the file) and dropping these comment lines (Redis ACL files take no comments).
#
# default: disabled, so a connection without AUTH can run nothing ("NOAUTH Authentication required").
# surge:   the one application user (gateway rate limits and token denylist, booking holds). Every command except
#          the @dangerous category (FLUSHALL, KEYS, CONFIG, DEBUG, MONITOR, SHUTDOWN, …), plus INFO, which Spring
#          Boot's Redis health check needs.
user default off resetpass resetkeys resetchannels -@all
user surge on #@@REDIS_SURGE_SHA256@@ ~* &* +@all -@dangerous +info
